# Text files check out with LF on every OS. Without this, a Windows checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true on the runner image) turns every text file into CRLF, and
# any test that cuts a committed file on '\n' fails there and only there:
# explain-static did on every Windows run from 2026-10-31 until d876bf5.
# Binary files (glb, png, mp4, ...) are detected by content and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
